cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its corpus, please cite it."
title: "agentmeld: one source of truth for AI coding-agent configuration"
abstract: >-
  agentmeld keeps one source of truth for the natural-language configuration an AI coding
  agent reads, and mirrors it into every vendor location: a one-line import where a tool can
  be told to read another file, a symlink or generated file where it cannot, a surgical merge
  into shared config such as MCP server declarations, and a per-tool overlay for guidance that
  is deliberately specific to one tool. Adapters are declarative TOML carrying a confidence
  field, so a path not confirmed against primary vendor documentation is excluded from the
  default sync. The design follows a measurement rather than an assumption: in a stratified
  sample of 1,905 public repositories carrying a root AGENTS.md, 649 also carry a CLAUDE.md,
  and of those pairs 40% are two genuinely distinct documents while 44% already point one file
  at the other. Mirroring one file over another would therefore destroy work about as often as
  it would save any, which is why the shared base and the per-tool difference are kept apart.
  The repository includes the mining script and the classified pair dataset.
